{"ts": 1791256746.1990871, "type": "step", "step": 18, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Short answer on attention: include it if it changes the agent\u2019s behavior or learning process in a way that matters to your build; otherwise treat it as a hidden factor and mention it briefly under limitations/assumptions. A safe write-up is: 'We model environment state, observations, and actions explicitly; attention is not directly observed, but because it can gate what the learner processes, we treat it as a latent variable that may affect learning outcomes.' If you send me your exact environment description, I\u2019ll help you decide whether attention belongs in the main state or in the caveats section.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-environments-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=12 messages 2m", "t": 14, "activity": [{"t": 12, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.4522004989181872, "pomdp": 0.3335520353737326, "pass_k": 0.27998147170370613}, "p_perf": {"attention": 1.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8430104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.34481971324228816, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
